---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import CagrCalculator from '@/components/tools/calc/CagrCalculator.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="cagr-calculator">
  <CagrCalculator client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the CAGR calculator works</h2>
    <p>
      The CAGR calculator finds the compound annual growth rate: the one yearly rate that takes the start
      value to the end value in the given number of years. It can also work the other way, from a start
      value and a rate to an end value.
    </p>
    <p>
      The formula is <code>CAGR = (End ÷ Start)^(1 ÷ years) − 1</code>. The reverse is
      <code>End = Start × (1 + CAGR)^years</code>. Years can be decimals, so 18 months is 1.5.
    </p>
    <h2>Worked example</h2>
    <p>
      An investment grows from 10,000 to 19,000 in 3 years. The multiple is 1.9 and the total growth is 90%.
      The CAGR is (1.9)^(1 ÷ 3) − 1 = 23.86% a year. The simple average, 90% ÷ 3, is 30%, which is higher
      because it ignores compounding. In reverse, 10,000 growing 8% a year for 3 years ends at 12,597.12.
    </p>
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
      CAGR is a smooth rate. The real value can go up and down between the start and the end. Money added or
      taken out in between is not counted; for that, use the IRR calculator.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
